## Exchanger
uplink-exchange-doubloon1-name = Iron Doubloon
uplink-exchange-doubloon1-desc = An iron coin with a value of 1 doubloon, used for small exchanges.
uplink-exchange-doubloon15-name = Silver Doubloon
uplink-exchange-doubloon15-desc = A silver coin with a value of 15 doubloons; highly prized among pirates.
uplink-exchange-doubloon50-name = Gold Doubloon
uplink-exchange-doubloon50-desc = A gold coin with a value of 50 doubloons—rare and expensive.
uplink-exchange-doubloon100-name = Diamond Doubloon
uplink-exchange-doubloon100-desc = A doubloon engraved onto a solid diamond, valued at 100 doubloons—an extremely valuable and prestigious coin.

## Weapons
uplink-weapon-scrap-name = SKM-24 "Scavenger" Kit
uplink-weapon-scrap-desc = An assault rifle kit that has clearly seen better days. It comes with a pair of magazines containing a mix of homemade and armor-piercing rounds. There is a chance the rifle might explode in your hands, but at this price, it's practically a free fireworks show.
uplink-weapon-base-name = SKM-24 Kit
uplink-weapon-base-desc = A kit for the rookie mercenary. The weapon comes straight from the warehouse, and the magazines are standardized — though the suppliers change more often than socks. It is reliable and definitely won't blow up in your hands.
uplink-weapon-arg-name = ARG Kit
uplink-weapon-arg-desc = A kit containing an old Galactic Standard Assault Rifle—a weapon still used to this day by various paramilitary groups and former militias.
uplink-weapon-crate-mosin-desc = A large wooden crate straight from the USSP's armories. Inside lie four weapons of endless trench warfare. The Kardashev-Mosin fires 7.62x54R rifle cartridges.
## Mech
uplink-mech-teleporter-pirate-name = Mining Exosuit
uplink-mech-teleporter-pirate-desc = A heavy mech designed for the harsh conditions of deep space. This "Bruiser" model is equipped with built-in thrusters and an industrial mining drill.

uplink-mech-teleporter-ussp-name = Assault Exosuit
uplink-mech-teleporter-ussp-desc = A heavy USSP combat exosuit based on the "Durand" chassis. The pinnacle of what one can acquire from the military surplus stockpiles of the USSP. Slow, but inexorable. Armed with an aging heavy machine gun.


uplink-piratedeathrattle-implant-desc = A box containing enough "Death Rattle" implants to supply an entire crew. It transmits a message containing your coordinates over the Freelance radio channel whenever you enter a critical state or die.
# Wearables
uplink-messenger-random-name = Spacious Messenger Bag
uplink-messenger-random-desc = A bag that strikes the perfect balance between carrying capacity and ease of access—ideal for stashing loot and tools for committing war crimes!
uplink-eva-bundle-name = "Scavenger" EVA Suit
uplink-eva-bundle-desc = A battered suit, held together with duct tape—but it offers protection. Just the thing for the price.
uplink-eva-armored-bundle-name = "Scavenger" Armored Boarding Suit
uplink-eva-armored-bundle-desc = A battered suit, covered in duct tape and patches. Worn over it is a layer of soft armor—just as full of holes, but it can still take a hit.
uplink-scaf-bundle-name = EVA Suit
uplink-scaf-bundle-desc = A green-and-brown EVA suit favored by pirates and mercenaries. It offers weak protection against lasers, but is nearly impervious to bullets. Designed for a quick getaway when things go south.
uplink-eva-pirate-bundle-name = Pirate EVA Suit
uplink-eva-bundle-desc = An iconic pirate getup straight out of the "Old Space" era. It offers protection on par with a Captain's suit—albeit at the cost of speed—and features a detachable EVA helmet with absolutely no flash protection.
# Cyber
uplink-throver-arm = "Rambler" Wrist Grenade Launcher
uplink-throver-arm-desc = Keep an ace up your sleeve! The Rambler can fire most types of grenades—excluding artillery rounds—as well as shotgun shells and anti-materiel rounds. Firing it generates a powerful recoil that knocks you off balance. (Warning: Requires surgical assistance.)
uplink-hack-arm = "NetRunner" Cyber-Arm
uplink-hack-arm-desc = An arm equipped with every tool needed to breach airlocks—and hack just about anything else you can get your hands on. A specialized device based on a multitool allows you to identify the function of specific wires. It offers no protection against electric shock. (Warning: Requires surgical assistance.)
uplink-atmos-arm = "Atmosian" Cyber-Arm
uplink-atmos-arm-desc = An arm containing a set of tools for repairing and patching hull breaches, as well as restoring atmospheric integrity from scratch. For certified Atmos Techs only! (Warning: Requires surgical assistance.)
uplink-ripper-arm = "Ripper" Cyber-Arm
uplink-ripper-arm-desc = It seems that having a surgical license—along with any concerns regarding sanitation—take a backseat for the patient when you operate on them using this implant. (Warning: Requires surgical assistance.)
uplink-mechwright-arm = "Mechanic" Cyber-Arm
uplink-mechwright-arm-desc = A set of tools is built directly into the arm. Congratulations: you have officially moved one step closer to becoming a cyborg; don't forget to recite your Laws on command. (Warning: Requires surgical assistance.)
# Disruption
uplink-pirate-fab-name = Pirate Fabricator
uplink-pirate-fab-desc = A penny saved is a penny earned; acquire your very own fabricator to print basic ammunition and medical supplies from tools. The "resource-optimized" version sacrifices speed for the sake of resource conservation.
# ally
uplink-base-scooner-name = Hire Freelancer
uplink-base-scooner-desc = Hire and summon — directly to your location — a pirate willing to join your venture; comes equipped with basic gear.
uplink-scrapper-scooner-name = Hire Scrapper
uplink-scrapper-scooner-desc = Hire and summon — directly to your location — a member of a Scrapper gang who may agree to join your venture; comes equipped with basic gear and a few doubloons.
